<newsitem itemid="14133" id="root" date="1996-08-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gencor raises yr shr and div.</title>
<headline>Gencor raises yr shr and div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-exceps (cts)     103.1   vs 73.8</p>
<p>    Shr, post-exceps (cts)    124.4   vs 72.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			25     vs 20</p>
<p>    Attrib income	     1,803     vs 1,003</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     2,719     vs 1,510</p>
<p>    Tax			     481     vs 419</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 105     vs 375</p>
<p>    Turnover		   13,241     vs 10,368</p>
<p>    Exceptional gain	    371     vs 17 loss</p>
<p>Full name: Gencor Ltd</p>
<p>Div payable September 27</p>
<p>On register September 13</p>
<p>NOTE - The consensus earnings per share forecast of analysts polled by Reuters was 93.12 cents, with the range 92.0-94.5. The dividend was forecast at 25.75 cents, with the range 25.0-27.0.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
